        "notes": "Running\nAsk pupils to answer both questions independently. Then take answers from the class and check that they use details from the lesson.\n\nAnswers\n1. A bakery on Pudding Lane, in London.\n2. Some people used a boat to escape.\n\nMisconceptions\nPupils may name St Paul’s Cathedral because it was destroyed, rather than where the fire began. Remind them that it began in a bakery on Pudding Lane. They may say people escaped by carrying belongings; Pepys described people carrying belongings away by boat.\n\nBackground\nPepys’s diary is an eyewitness account because he saw events himself and wrote about them.",
